// Copyright DreamMoon. All Rights Reserved.
//
// The sky cloud renderer (FDreamSkyCloudViewExtension): per view, after the base pass,
//   MarchCS     one ray per Downsample x Downsample pixels through the cloud layer (DreamSkyCloudShape.ush), stepped by
//               the shared march (DreamCloudMarch.ush): skipping clear air -- by a true lower bound of the distance near
//               and above the layer, where only cumulonimbus stand; by a step in the layer, backing off to walk fine
//               when a skip lands where cloud may be --, fine steps no longer than a billow near a surface, offset per
//               pixel and frame (the steps' banding turns into noise the history averages away). Toon: the surface,
//               refined, then read around and painted in the style's tones exactly as the dome's toon march does
//               (DSky_WalkSurface, DSky_PaintSurface). Realistic: the density integrated along the ray, lit by scattering
//               (DreamCloudLight.ush). The dome's weather haze goes on the clouds here (the dome hazes its own sky).
//   SunMapCS    the optical depth toward the sun at every texel of a box round the view (two cascades, 10 km tall over
//               the layer's base): what the realistic clouds are shadowed by, read once a sample instead of looking
//               toward the light from each.
//   PanoramaCS  the clouds round the view, longitude by latitude, every fourth frame: what the dome shows in the sky light
//               capture (the capture renders no base pass and calls no view extension).
//   ShadowCS    the clouds' shadow on the ground: the sun map's transmittance from the layer's base toward the sun, which
//               the sun light's light function (M_DreamCloudShadow) reads.
//   TemporalCS  the previous frames' clouds reprojected by the clouds' depth (the sky at infinity by the rotation alone),
//               clamped to the new frame's neighbourhood, blended in.
//   CompositePS the clouds over the sky pixels (premultiplied: the sky behind times their transmittance plus their
//               light), bilinear from the reduced resolution: the clouds stand behind everything the depth buffer holds,
//               so every texel a sky pixel reads is a sky ray. DebugMode 1 instead multiplies the sky by a grid of view
//               directions (15 degree lines, the horizon band red).
//   LightShaftsCS  the sunlight the air below the layer scatters toward the view where the clouds' shadow lets it
//               through (the ground shadow ShadowCS draws), at the rays' resolution: shafts through the gaps of broken
//               clouds. LightShaftsCompositePS adds it over the scene before the post processing.
//   CompositeBelowPS  with the view over the layer's base, the clouds between it and the scene, over the scene, before
//               the post processing (after the fog and the translucency: a cloud then covers the rain, particles and glass in
//               front of it). Upsampled taking only the rays whose clouds stand nearer than the pixel's scene.

